# Change log

Changes are recorded newest first. Dates use YYYY-MM-DD.

## 2026-11-14 — Introduce ongoing change tracking

- Added this root `change.log` as the package's ongoing change record, with a
  narrowly scoped `.gitignore` exception; operational logs remain ignored.
- Added an `AGENTS.md` rule requiring a change-log update with every package
  change, including documentation and project guidance, and recording relevant
  GitHub repository-setting changes when applied.
- The rule requires truthful validation evidence, preservation of prior history,
  and a clear distinction between source publication and live deployment.
- Scope: documentation only; no runtime behavior, settings, existing reports, or
  live installation changed.
- Validation: `git diff --check` passed; all 197 offline unit tests passed with
  Python 3.12.14 (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -q`);
  existing roadmap guidance preserved.

## Earlier history

This log begins with the change-tracking update. It is not a retrospective record
of every earlier change. The Git history is the authoritative record for work
before this file was introduced; the immediately preceding commit is
`cd26e01470d2edb7a3541fa522242b7cdec19b21` (community policies and contribution
templates).
